  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZPP - Strengthening Civil Society Engagement and Participation in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZPP works to attain sustainable peace in Zimbabwe where there is peace, justice, dignity and development for all. This is through monitoring, documentation, advocacy and community peace building interventions with members and partners. The organisation mainstreams disability, gender, safeguarding and monitoring, evaluation, accountability and learning.&#xa0;&#xa0;The work of ZPP is guided by the following four strategic drivers:&#xa0;To contribute towards building a Zimbabwean citizenry that demands Human Rights accountability&#xa0;-&#xa0;ZPP focuses on the monitoring and documentation of human rights violations and works with 470 community-based monitors. They monitor the whole spectrum of human rights violations that include civil, political, social, economic and cultural rights. The monitoring work is evidence based, triangulated and verified through ZPPs three-tier verification protocol and by other like-minded and community-based organisations (CBOs) and civil society organisations (CSOs) nationwide. The violation reports are collated to produce a Monthly Monitoring Reporting (MMR) which is a flagship product of the organization. Supplementary to the MMR, the organization also generates other advocacy publications informed by the monitoring reports from the monitors. These reports are but not limited to, fact sheets, position papers, special reports, discussion papers, weekly editions to mention a few.</narrative>
  </description>
